10.4 Interface with Identifiability

The equivalence margin for the memory-side test is

\delta_I = \eta_I \cdot R_C(\varepsilon), \qquad \eta_I = 0.1.

For \mathbf p_A and \varepsilon = 0.10, \delta_I = 0.102 bits. The observed change \Delta I is declared equivalent if |\Delta I| < 0.102 bits. This makes the equivalence margin task-relative rather than arbitrary.

