5. Monotonicity and convexity of R_C(D).
6. Boundary conditions R_C(0) = H(C) and R_C(D_{\max}) = 0.

The earlier claim of validation was insufficient because it did not include an independent numerical check of the three-class non-uniform case.

E.5 Interface with Identifiability

The equivalence margin for the memory-side test is

\delta_I = \eta_I \cdot R_C(\varepsilon), \qquad \eta_I = 0.1.

For \mathbf p_A and \varepsilon = 0.10, \delta_I = 0.102 bits. The observed change \Delta I is declared equivalent if |\Delta I| < 0.102 bits. This makes the equivalence margin task-relative rather than arbitrary. Sensitivity analysis is required over

\eta_I \in \{0.05, 0.10, 0.20\}, \qquad \eta_D \in \{0.05, 0.10, 0.20\}.

